<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Afrighid Khwarazm</h1><p class="st-meta">305 CE – 995 CE (approx.) · capital Kath</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The native dynasty of Khwarazm for nearly seven centuries, whose shahs kept the region's Iranian culture alive through Arab conquest and Samanid overlordship.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>According to the Khwarazmian scholar al-Biruni, the Afrighid dynasty was founded by Afrig in 305 CE, succeeding the older royal house of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-khwarazm">Kingdom of Khwarazm</a>. Afrig built a fortress at Kath on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxus">Amu Darya</a>, which became the capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The shahs ruled an irrigated land of canals, towns and fortified manors that traded north with the steppe and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zoroastrianism">Zoroastrianism</a> and the Khwarazmian language and calendar persisted. After the Arab general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qutayba-ibn-muslim">Qutayba ibn Muslim</a> conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazm">Khwarazm</a> in 712, the shahs remained as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>, converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and ruled under Caliphal and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samanid-empire">Samanid</a> authority, while a rival centre grew at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurganj">Gurganj</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 995 the emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurganj">Gurganj</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamun-ibn-muhammad">Ma'mun ibn Muhammad</a>, overthrew and killed the last Afrighid shah, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-abdallah-muhammad-afrighid">Abu Abdallah Muhammad</a>, and founded <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mamunid-khwarazm">Ma'munid Khwarazm</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-biruni">Al-Biruni</a>, born near Kath, preserved much of what is known of the dynasty.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/afrighid-khwarazm.jpg" alt="Afrighid Khwarazm" width="320" height="198"><figcaption>Image: Edited by HistoryofIran, originally work by Gabagool · CC BY 1.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AfrighidsMap.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>305 CE – 995 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kath</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Afrig, Abu Abdallah Muhammad</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Zoroastrianism, later Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Khwarazmian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>, <a href="/countries/turkmenistan">Turkmenistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Afrighid dynasty, Khwarazmshahs (Afrighid)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=650&amp;focus=afrighid-khwarazm" aria-label="Afrighid Khwarazm on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6160 693 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Afrighid Khwarazm lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6480 949L6469 949M6480 949L6134 1224M6480 949L6588 1010"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6469 949h0M6134 1224h0M6588 1010h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6480 949h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6480 949h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=650&amp;focus=afrighid-khwarazm">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
